    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 5.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.4">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5.4" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ se þe þæt nelle, þæt his hade gebyrige, wanige his weorðscipe ægðer ge for Gode ge for worolde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And se þe þæt nelle þæt his hade gebyrige, wanige his weorðscipe ægðer ge for Gode ge for worolde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And he who will not do what befits his order shall impair both his ecclesiastical and his civil status.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And he who will not act in a manner fitting for his order shall diminish his honor before God and the world.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Dagegen wer das ablehnt, was seinem geistlichen Stande ziemt: schwinde sein Ehrenrang so in der Kirche wie im Weltlichen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But whoever refuses what befits his holy order: let his honour diminish both in the Church and in the world.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="248">V Atr 9.[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 9,[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_29">VIII Atr 29</ref></note>
      </div>
